1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,319
You're an idiot for buying one lottery ticket.

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:04,642
This guy's team bought over five million.

3
00:00:05,092 --> 00:00:12,519
Virginia, nineteen ninety-two. Seven million and fifty-nine thousand possible combinations. One dollar each.

4
00:00:12,819 --> 00:00:18,539
The jackpot? Twenty-seven million. So a fund from Australia did the math. Buy every single one.

5
00:00:18,838 --> 00:00:20,431
Hit like if you'd have done it too.

6
00:00:20,731 --> 00:00:26,737
But buying them takes time. They ran out of it, with about one and a half million combinations never bought.

7
00:00:27,038 --> 00:00:29,809
Send this to the friend who still plays their birthday.

8
00:00:30,109 --> 00:00:32,331
Follow along. Then the numbers came out.

9
00:00:32,731 --> 00:00:35,570
Eight. Eleven. Thirteen. Fifteen. Nineteen. Twenty.

10
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:38,289
They had it. Twenty-seven million dollars.

11
00:00:38,740 --> 00:00:46,072
Today, Powerball has two hundred ninety-two million combinations. At one ticket a second, that's nine years of printing.

12
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:48,962
So yes. You're still an idiot for buying one.
